mode on is a new operating point.

Relay-BP implements T. Müller et al., "Improved Belief Propagation Is Sufficient for Real-Time
Decoding of Quantum Memory", arXiv:2506.01779 (2025), doi:10.48550/arXiv.2506.01779.
IBM's reference implementation relay_bp / relay-bp (version 0.2.2), (C) Copyright IBM 2025,
is licensed under Apache-2.0 (https://github.com/trmue/relay). No code was copied or translated
from relay_bp; the port implements the published algorithm with eldpc's existing CUDA kernel.
The gamma draws differ (SplitMix64 here versus StdRng in relay_bp), and relay_legs includes the
initial leg, whereas relay_bp's num_sets counts subsequent legs. The comparison tools call
relay_bp at run time; it is not vendored, linked or redistributed. It is installed separately
under its own Apache-2.0 licence.
